defmodule VmuCoreWeb.Icons do
  @moduledoc """
  The admin console's icon set — an inline SVG `<symbol>` sprite plus an
  `<.icon name="..."/>` component that references it with `<use>`.

  ## Why a sprite

  This app has no asset pipeline (no npm, no esbuild, no icon font), so an
  icon library is not installable. Emoji were the previous answer; they render
  differently on every platform and cannot take the surrounding text colour,
  which makes accent-tinted navigation impossible.

  A sprite solves both without a build step: the symbol definitions are
  emitted once per page by `sprite/1`, and each use site is a four-attribute
  `<use>` that inherits `currentColor`. Adding an icon means adding one
  `<symbol>` here.

  Paths follow Heroicons v2 *outline* geometry — 24×24 viewBox, no fill,
  1.5px stroke, round caps and joins — so glyphs stay optically consistent
  with each other and with the reference design this console follows.

  ## Usage

      <.sprite />                          <%!-- once, just inside <body> --%>
      <.icon name="credit-card" />
      <.icon name="bolt" class="vp-icon-lg" />

  An unknown name renders the `minus-small` fallback rather than raising: a
  typo should cost one glyph, not the whole navigation.
  """

